From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gas: testsuite: exclude microblazeel from the diff1 test

gas/all/gas.exp skips "difference of two undefined symbols" for targets that
resolve such differences at link time via relaxation, MicroBlaze among them
(the comment lists it).  The guard is "microblaze-*-*", which matches the
big-endian triplet but not the little-endian "microblazeel-*-*", so the test
runs and fails on microblazeel even though the assembler behaves correctly.
Widen the glob to "microblaze*-*-*", covering both endiannesses -- the same
shape the AVR/RL78/RX entries already use.

gas/ChangeLog:
	* testsuite/gas/all/gas.exp: Exclude microblaze*-*-* (both
	endiannesses) from diff1, not just microblaze-*-*.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/gas/testsuite/gas/all/gas.exp b/gas/testsuite/gas/all/gas.exp
index 46451fb5a..7782fd411 100644
--- a/gas/testsuite/gas/all/gas.exp
+++ b/gas/testsuite/gas/all/gas.exp
@@ -70,7 +70,7 @@ if {    ![istarget alpha*-*-*vms*]
      && ![istarget avr-*-*]
      && ![istarget ft32-*-*]
      && ![istarget hppa*-*-*]
-     && ![istarget microblaze-*-*]
+     && ![istarget microblaze*-*-*]
      && ![istarget loongarch*-*-*]
      && ![istarget mn10300-*-*]
      && ![istarget msp430*-*-*]
